Subject: [PATCH] venus: refuse a dma-buf import when the renderer has none (vtest)

The vtest renderer sets bo_ops.create_from_dma_buf to NULL, but
vn_renderer_bo_create_from_dma_buf calls it without a check. Any dma-buf import then calls
address 0: vkGetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR (vn_get_memory_dma_buf_properties) and
vkAllocateMemory with VkImportMemoryFdInfoKHR. Our WSI patch 0004 (the direct present to the
app) calls vkGetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR for each of the app's buffers when the swapchain is
made. On Arm's Mali-G715 driver, Wine's first OpenGL call faulted there, inside
win32u's pthread_once for the OpenGL driver; Wine returned the fault to the caller, the once
stayed "in progress", and the game's next OpenGL call waited on it for ever (no frame).
With no import op, return VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE; the direct present then keeps
PutImage ("the GPU refused a buffer").

Applied by build-sysdrv.sh to its Venus build of Mesa main (config.sh MESA_COMMIT) only.

---
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer.h
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer.h
@@ -331,6 +331,10 @@ vn_renderer_bo_create_from_dma_buf(struc
                                    VkMemoryPropertyFlags flags,
                                    struct vn_renderer_bo **out_bo)
 {
+   /* PD2 Launcher: the vtest renderer has no dma-buf import (NULL op) */
+   if (!renderer->bo_ops.create_from_dma_buf)
+      return VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
+
    struct vn_renderer_bo *bo;
    VkResult result =
       renderer->bo_ops.create_from_dma_buf(renderer, size, fd, flags, &bo);
